{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06GB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-essential-surjection}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:213045757e75c8407ab6756183e9613e467276553d7871e7904617aba6337fb8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:64d9d9049d56654f15914a0be359ba86c5f66053657dd30b2d48102bea444bd5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNext we define essential surjections in <MATH_0001>. A necessary\nand sufficient condition for a surjection in <MATH_0002> to be\nessential is given in Lemma <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:602ac89fa38d11b7367106d315509c8befd6d5bbbaf64c6d2e5a830a74b13912", "unit_id": "tag:06GB:prose-0008"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06GB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f: B \\to A$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$g: C \\to B$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0007": "$f \\circ g$", "MATH_0008": "$g$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-essential-surjection}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e870fd7fe45872ad1632340ed10dcf7a80b5aa1284f2c8a20c30e96c393bf03a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8d6e7d833cd91d53ee83336d6bcc6ef489da439ffeb16c77aefeb8a5fb3cd933", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ring map in <MATH_0002>.  We say <MATH_0003>\nis an <TEXTITOPEN_0001>essential surjection<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if it has the following properties:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is surjective.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0005> is a ring map in <MATH_0006> such that\n<MATH_0007> is surjective, then <MATH_0008> is surjective.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2b5a63cd22fdafa1c04aa7df672784e14d316777a15bc378d9341467eb46b0f4", "unit_id": "tag:06GF:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06GB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-surjective}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fb6ad280346362a580dd3b1ba5464da5eea3146f40ecf0a8f3a682476d6fa006", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:80c42a6b316ecb1d421e837a0132d1e07c2870932d94b18399616645b80ffcb6", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nUsing Lemma <REF_0001>, we can characterize\nessential surjections in <MATH_0001> as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b4e725b9602538548135c0595777077b7aff2eb25744ac91b95581513630e714", "unit_id": "tag:06GB:prose-0009"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06GB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f: B \\to A$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$B/\\mathfrak m_B^2 \\to A/\\mathfrak m_A^2$", "MATH_0005": "$B/(\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda B + \\mathfrak m_B^2) \\to\nA/(\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda A + \\mathfrak m_A^2)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-essential-surjection-mod-squares}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:281237f7766fcacb037ce35d9be0c688dd4dcdebf1f815be24abc9a90dfe87b2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cd25ec67d81d6e5b34d5509244a18fbf835643c4c4f4108015e0862aa1a57795", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ring map in <MATH_0002>.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> is an essential surjection,\n<STRUCT_0003> the map <MATH_0004> is an essential\nsurjection, and\n<STRUCT_0004> the map\n<MATH_0005> is an essential surjection.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ef435beec1df81fb8556250ac67a0fb9ce3356e29ab1b132a0247b38e4c8ca67", "unit_id": "tag:06S5:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06GB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$C \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$C \\to A$", "MATH_0004": "$C \\to A/(\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda A + \\mathfrak m_A^2)$", "MATH_0005": "$C \\to B/(\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda B + \\mathfrak m_B^2)$", "MATH_0006": "$C \\to B$", "MATH_0007": "$C \\to B/(\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda B + \\mathfrak m_B^2)$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0009": "$C \\to A/(\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda A + \\mathfrak m_A^2)$", "MATH_0010": "$C' = C \\times_{B/(\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda B + \\mathfrak m_B^2)} B$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0012": "$C' \\to A/(\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda A + \\mathfrak m_A^2)$", "MATH_0013": "$C' \\to A$", "MATH_0014": "$C' \\to B$", "MATH_0015": "$C' \\to B/(\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda B + \\mathfrak m_B^2)$", "MATH_0016": "$C'$", "MATH_0017": "$C \\to B/(\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda B + \\mathfrak m_B^2)$", "MATH_0018": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0019": "$\\Rightarrow$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-surjective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-fiber-product-CLambda}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-surjective}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:809abad8c624a309e627e58d5a3d4a88ab74ab92481d042d9fa65a093dedbc06", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1520dc1d1741385e103aa0202d86c6a55fd52ac310870ef6810cfd88d558e4ed", "source_text": "Assume (3). Let <MATH_0001> be a ring map in <MATH_0002> such\nthat <MATH_0003> is surjective. Then\n<MATH_0004> is surjective\ntoo. We conclude that <MATH_0005>\nis surjective by our assumption. Hence <MATH_0006> is surjective by applying\nLemma <REF_0001> (2 times).\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nAssume (1). Let <MATH_0007>\nbe a morphism of <MATH_0008> such that\n<MATH_0009> is surjective. Set\n<MATH_0010>\nwhich is an object of <MATH_0011> by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nNote that <MATH_0012>\nis still surjective, hence <MATH_0013> is surjective by\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nThus <MATH_0014> is surjective by our assumption. This implies\nthat <MATH_0015> is\nsurjective, which implies by the construction of <MATH_0016> that\n<MATH_0017> is surjective.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nIn the first paragraph we proved (3) <MATH_0018> (1) and in the second\nparagraph we proved (1) <MATH_0019> (3). The equivalence of\n(2) and (3) is a special case of the equivalence of (1) and (3), hence\nwe are done.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f648f5b5175e4b4dcbdb6ed9bd2a38177fd007a04d901f60336d551b526ca6f8", "unit_id": "tag:06S5:proof"}
